## The `help:` line for a `native.subset.1` problem (ADR 0722). The problem's
## message is written by `lower.ail` and its siblings; this file only reads it,
## so the messages can change without touching the lowering. Native is the only
## backend (ADR 0904), so a refused construct has no other route: the help says
## how to write it with what is built.

## The help text for a message (native.subset.1 names the construct and the position; this line
## says what to do). A message with no entry gets the generic line. An internal error has no help.
pub fn subset_help(message str) str
    if message.starts_with("internal error")
        return ""
    h := entry_help(message)
    if h == ""
        return "rewrite it with plain functions, structs, enums, lists, maps and loops; the other errors name what else is missing"
    h

## The help text for a message, or "" when no entry matches. The first match
## wins, so the more specific forms come first.
fn entry_help(message str) str
    if message.contains("comprehension whose type isn't known")
        or message.contains("a comprehension whose element type isn't known")
        return "give the list its type with `List[T]()` and `push` in a loop"
    if message.contains("maps")
        or message.contains("Map[")
        or message.contains("a map of")
        or message.contains("a key of type")
        return "maps are native with `int`, `bool`, `char` or `str` keys (ADR 0568); `get` and `remove` need `else`; other keys aren't built"
    if message.contains("this `else` must leave")
        return "write `else return`, `else break`, `else continue`, or a fallback value"
    if message.contains("`for mut`")
        return "loop by index instead: `for i in 0..xs.len()` and `xs[i] = ...`"
    if message.contains("printing a `")
        return "print the fields you need, for example `print(v.x)`"
    if message.contains("`path` isn't in the native subset yet")
        or message.contains("isn't in the native subset yet (only locals, parameters and constants)")
        return "a module-level value that isn't a constant can't be read here; pass it as a parameter"
    ""
